# `''` in a verbatim string: no escapes there, so the fix switches quotes.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where customerId != @'it''s'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..44
  PIPELINE@0..43
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..43
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..43
        NAME_REF@21..31
          IDENT@21..31 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
        NEQ@32..34 "!="
        WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
        LITERAL@35..43
          STRING@35..40 "@'it'"
          STRING@40..43 "'s'"
  WHITESPACE@43..44 "\n"

error[DS0117]: `''` does not put a quote in a string
  --> query:1:40
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where customerId != @'it''s'
  |                                        ^^ this ends the string and starts another
  |
  = help: a verbatim string has no escapes; use the other quote: `@"it's"`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where customerId != @"it's"
which parses without errors
